    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649-a1">

                <pb facs="0828" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg716"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Mexico</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-17T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>985. See Consul Dawson’s April 14, 6 p.m., and April 15, 7 p.m. Bring situation
                    in oil fields as reported therein to attention <pb facs="0829" n="717"
                        xml:id="pg717"/> Mexican Government, and urgently request it to take prompt
                    steps to extend protection to American life and property in oil fields. Insist
                    upon vigorous action and telegraph result.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
